# 

**Release Date:** August 14, 2026 | **Status:** General Availability

---

## 🎉 Release Summary

CloudSync v2.5 is a major release bringing multi-cloud support, significant performance improvements (40% faster sync operations), and critical stability fixes. This release enables customers to manage AWS, Azure, and Google Cloud resources from a unified console while maintaining the highest reliability standards.

**Key Highlights:**
- ✨ Multi-cloud provider support (AWS, Azure, GCP)
- 🚀 40% performance improvement in sync operations
- 🔒 Critical bug fixes for concurrent operations
- ↩️ Full backward compatibility maintained

---

## ✨ New Features

### Multi-Cloud Provider Support
Add support for AWS, Azure, and Google Cloud Platform in a unified console. Customers can manage cloud resources across multiple providers from a single dashboard.

**GitHub Epic:** [KAN-1](https://anubhutishri123.atlassian.net/browse/KAN-1)

### Unified Console for Cloud Management
Single dashboard for viewing and managing all cloud resources across providers. Eliminates the need to switch between provider dashboards.

**GitHub Epic:** [KAN-2](https://anubhutishri123.atlassian.net/browse/KAN-2)

### Real-Time Sync Optimization
The optimized sync engine enables real-time data synchronization for large datasets. Enables sync up to 10x faster than the previous version.

**GitHub Epic:** [KAN-3](https://anubhutishri123.atlassian.net/browse/KAN-3)

---

## 🚀 Performance Improvements

### Sync Performance Enhancement
Overall sync speed improved 40% across all data types through algorithm optimization.
- **Impact:** 45 seconds → 27 seconds for typical 10GB datasets
- **Concurrency:** 5–10x more simultaneous operations supported
- **Issue:** [KAN-4](https://anubhutishri123.atlassian.net/browse/KAN-4)

### API Latency Reduction
Reduced API latency by optimizing query paths and connection pooling.
- **Impact:** 35% improvement in average response times
- **P99 Latency:** Reduced by 45%
- **Issue:** [KAN-5](https://anubhutishri123.atlassian.net/browse/KAN-5)

### Memory Usage Optimization
Optimized memory usage for high-concurrency scenarios.
- **Impact:** 30% reduction in memory footprint
- **Benefit:** Better performance when multiple users sync simultaneously
- **Issue:** [KAN-6](https://anubhutishri123.atlassian.net/browse/KAN-6)

---

## 🔧 Bug Fixes

### Race Condition in Concurrent Updates — **CRITICAL**
Fixed a race condition that could occur when multiple updates happened simultaneously. Eliminates occasional sync conflicts in high-concurrency scenarios.

**Severity:** Critical | **Status:** Verified
**Issue:** [KAN-7](https://anubhutishri123.atlassian.net/browse/KAN-7)

### Network Timeout Error Handling
Improved error messages and automatic retry logic when the network is unavailable. Users receive clear feedback when network issues occur; automatic retry reduces manual intervention.

**Severity:** High | **Status:** Verified
**Issue:** [KAN-8](https://anubhutishri123.atlassian.net/browse/KAN-8)

### Sync Conflict Resolution
Resolved sync conflicts that occurred in high-concurrency data updates. Improved sync reliability and data consistency.

**Severity:** High | **Status:** Verified
**Issue:** [KAN-9](https://anubhutishri123.atlassian.net/browse/KAN-9)

---

## 📋 Breaking Changes

### Python Version Requirement Updated
**Effective:** August 14, 2026

Minimum Python version requirement updated from **Python 3.6 to Python 3.8**.

**Why:**
- Python 3.6 and 3.7 reached end-of-life
- v2.5 uses Python 3.8+ features for performance improvements
- Aligns with industry standards

**Migration:**
```bash
# Check your current version
python --version

# If < 3.8, upgrade via package manager
# Then deploy CloudSync v2.5
```

---

## 🔄 Deprecations

### OAuth 1.0 Authentication
**Status:** Deprecated (still works until December 31, 2026)

OAuth 1.0 is being phased out in favor of OAuth 2.0.

**Timeline:**
- **August 14, 2026:** OAuth 1.0 deprecated (still functional)
- **December 31, 2026:** OAuth 1.0 removed

**Action Required:** Migrate to OAuth 2.0 before December 31, 2026

---

## ⚠️ Known Issues

### Large File Import Timeout
**Issue:** Import of files >5GB may timeout

**Workaround:** Split large imports into smaller batches (< 5GB each)

**Expected Fix:** v2.6 (Q4 2026)

### Concurrent Import Limitations
**Issue:** Importing from multiple cloud providers simultaneously may be slow

**Workaround:** Import from one provider, wait for completion, then import from next provider

**Expected Fix:** v2.7 (Q1 2027)

---

## 🔒 Security Updates

- ✅ AES-256 Token Encryption for all session tokens
- ✅ Enhanced RBAC with custom permissions support
- ✅ Security Headers: HSTS, CSP, X-Frame-Options
- ✅ 32 dependency security patches applied
- ✅ Third-party penetration test: PASSED (zero vulnerabilities)
- ✅ SOC 2 Type II certified
- ✅ GDPR & CCPA compliant

